module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.Grp.Limits
public import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.Grp.Zero
public import Mathlib.Algebra.Homology.ShortComplex.Ab
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.SheafCohomology.Cech
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.Whiskering
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.CechComplex
public import StacksFrontier.Topology.Sheaves.Cohomology.Locality.CohomologyVanishesLocally

/-!
# Vanishing of cohomology from Čech vanishing on a basis

Let `B` be a basis of open subsets of a space.  Stacks Tag 01EW asserts that if a cofinal
collection of covers by members of `B`, whose finite intersections also belong to `B`, has
vanishing positive-degree Čech cohomology, then higher sheaf cohomology vanishes on every member
of `B`.  This file sets up the statement and proves the degree-one case, which needs neither the
basis hypothesis nor the closure of `B` under the finite intersections: only the cofinality of
the collection of covers and the vanishing of degree-one Čech cohomology.

The development is **generic in the coefficients**: they are an abelian category `𝒜` with
enough injectives together with an exact functor `T` to the abelian sheaves on `X`, the
"underlying abelian sheaf" of a coefficient object.  Sheaves of modules over a sheaf of rings `R`
are the case `T = SheafOfModules.toSheaf R`, which is how Tag 01EW is stated in
`StacksDraft.Ch20.Sec11.Tag01EWCycles`; abelian sheaves themselves are the case `T = 𝟭`, which
is `StacksDraft.Ch20.Sec11.Tag01EWAbelian`.  Nothing beyond the exactness of `T` and the Čech
acyclicity of the sheaves underlying injective objects is used anywhere in the proof.

Every degree rests on a Čech-to-cohomology comparison built here by hand from an injective
resolution, `exists_sec_eq_of_cech_isZero`: degree `m + 1` of Tag 01EW follows from the
degree-one Čech vanishing for the object of `m`-cocycles of the resolution, see
`isZero_Hobj_succ_of_cech_isZero`.  For `m = 0` that object is `F` itself, so the degree-one
case is unconditional.  For `m > 0` the degree-one Čech vanishing for the cocycle objects is the
one input still missing, and `isZero_Hobj_of_cechCycles_isZero` is Tag 01EW with exactly that
input as a hypothesis.

## Main definitions

* `OpenCover` packages a family of open subsets covering a specified open subset, and
  `OpenCover.Refines` is refinement of open covers.
* `compactOpens` is the set of quasi-compact opens, the basis at which the criterion is
  instantiated on a space with a basis of quasi-compact opens.
* `CechCohomologyIsZero` expresses vanishing of Čech cohomology in one degree, for coefficients
  in a sheaf of modules.
* `res` is the restriction of a section of a presheaf of abelian groups along an inclusion of
  open subsets, `sec` is the map on sections induced by a morphism of coefficients, and
  `coverSieve` is the sieve generated by a family of open subsets.
* `abPresheaf T A` is the presheaf of abelian groups underlying a coefficient object,
  `secFunctor T W` is sections over `W` as a functor of the coefficients, `Hobj T W n` is its
  `n`-th right-derived functor and `secComplex T I W` is the complex of sections of an injective
  resolution.
* `cechMk` is the section of a term of the Čech complex with prescribed components.

## Main results

* `exists_res_eq_of_compatible` and `eq_of_res_eq` are the gluing and the separatedness
  statements for a sheaf of abelian groups on a topological space, in element form and with no
  restriction on the universe of the indexing type of the cover.
* `exists_map_eq_of_isLimit_kernelFork` says that a functor to abelian groups preserving kernels
  turns a kernel fork into an exact sequence of abelian groups; `exists_sec_eq_of_isLimit` is the
  instance of this for coefficients.
* `map_cocomplex_exactAt` says that an exact coefficient functor carries an injective resolution
  to a complex of abelian sheaves exact in positive degrees.
* `exists_cover_res_eq_d` extracts local primitives for a section killed by a differential of an
  injective resolution; it is the section-level form of Tag 01E3.
* `exists_sec_eq_of_cech_isZero` is the Čech-to-cohomology comparison in degree one, for the
  coefficients of an arbitrary kernel presentation `G ⟶ A ⟶ A'`: a section of `A'` which has
  local primitives on an open cover with vanishing degree-one Čech cohomology for `G` has a
  primitive over the whole open.
* `isZero_Hobj_succ_of_cech_isZero` deduces `Hᵐ⁺¹(U, F) = 0` from the degree-one Čech
  vanishing for the object of `m`-cocycles of an injective resolution.
* `isZero_Hobj_one_of_cech_isZero` is the degree-one case of Tag 01EW, and
  `isZero_Hobj_one_of_cech_isZero_on_basis` restates it with the hypotheses of the general
  statement of Tag 01EW.
* `isZero_Hobj_of_cechCycles_isZero` is Tag 01EW in every degree, modulo the single extra
  hypothesis that the degree-one Čech cohomology of the objects of cocycles of an injective
  resolution vanishes for the covers in `Cov`.

## Implementation notes

Čech cohomology is the homology of Mathlib's Čech complex of the underlying abelian-group
presheaf.  Vanishing of both Čech and sheaf cohomology is expressed categorically by `IsZero`.
The collection of covers is represented as a set of small open covers; its cofinality condition
explicitly says that each small cover has a refinement in the collection.

The gluing lemmas are stated through the sieve-theoretic sheaf condition rather than through
`TopCat.Sheaf.existsUnique_gluing`, because the latter needs the category of abelian groups to
have limits indexed by the universe of the topological space.

Sections are handled in the form `ToType ((abPresheaf T A).obj (op W))` throughout, rather than
`ToType ((secFunctor T W).obj A)`: the two are definitionally equal, but only the former is
matched syntactically by the restriction maps of the presheaf, and `rewrite` needs a syntactic
match.  Elements of the products occurring in the Čech complex are produced through `ofElt`,
which views a section as a morphism from the free abelian group on one generator; this avoids
assuming that the category of abelian groups has products indexed by the universe of the space.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01EW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01EW)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite TopologicalSpace
open Stacks.CategoryTheory.CechComplex

universe u₂ v₂ w v u

namespace Stacks.Cohomology.Basis

variable {X : Type u} [TopologicalSpace X]

/-! ### Open covers -/

/-- A small family of open subsets whose supremum is a specified open subset. -/
structure OpenCover (X : Type u) [TopologicalSpace X] where
  /-- The indexing type of the cover. -/
  ι : Type u
  /-- The open subset being covered. -/
  carrier : Opens X
  /-- The members of the cover. -/
  obj : ι → Opens X
  /-- The covering condition. -/
  iSup_eq : ⨆ i, obj i = carrier

namespace OpenCover

/-- `V.Refines U` means that `V` and `U` cover the same open and every member of `V` is
contained in a member of `U`. -/
def Refines (V U : OpenCover X) : Prop :=
  V.carrier = U.carrier ∧ ∀ j, ∃ i, V.obj j ≤ U.obj i

/-- Each member of an open cover is contained in the open subset it covers. -/
theorem obj_le (V : OpenCover X) (i : V.ι) : V.obj i ≤ V.carrier :=
  V.iSup_eq ▸ le_iSup V.obj i

end OpenCover

/-- The set of quasi-compact opens of `X`. This is the basis `B` at which the vanishing
criterion Stacks 01EW is instantiated on a space with a basis of quasi-compact opens. -/
def compactOpens (X : Type u) [TopologicalSpace X] : Set (Opens X) :=
  {V | IsCompact (V : Set X)}

/-- Vanishing in degree `n` of the Čech cohomology of an open cover with coefficients in a
sheaf of modules. -/
noncomputable def CechCohomologyIsZero
    (R : Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) RingCat) (F : SheafOfModules.{max u w} R)
    (U : OpenCover X) (n : ℕ) : Prop :=
  IsZero (((cechComplexFunctor U.obj).obj ((SheafOfModules.toSheaf R).obj F).obj).homology n)

/-! ### Restriction of sections -/

/-- Restriction of a section of a presheaf of abelian groups along an inclusion of opens. -/
def res (Q : (Opens X)ᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{v}) {V W : Opens X} (h : V ≤ W)
    (s : ToType (Q.obj (op W))) : ToType (Q.obj (op V)) :=
  ConcreteCategory.hom (Q.map (homOfLE h).op) s

variable (Q : (Opens X)ᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{v})

/-- Restriction along a morphism of opens is `res`. -/
theorem res_eq_apply {V W : Opens X} (f : V ⟶ W) (s : ToType (Q.obj (op W))) :
    ConcreteCategory.hom (Q.map f.op) s = res Q (leOfHom f) s := rfl

/-- Restricting along the identity does nothing. -/
@[simp]
theorem res_id {V : Opens X} (s : ToType (Q.obj (op V))) : res Q (le_refl V) s = s := by
  simp only [res, homOfLE_refl, op_id, Q.map_id, ConcreteCategory.id_apply]

/-- Restricting twice is restricting once. -/
theorem res_res {V W Y : Opens X} (h₁ : V ≤ W) (h₂ : W ≤ Y) (s : ToType (Q.obj (op Y))) :
    res Q h₁ (res Q h₂ s) = res Q (h₁.trans h₂) s := by
  simp only [res, ← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, ← Q.map_comp, ← op_comp]
  rfl

/-- Restriction is additive, so it preserves the zero section. -/
@[simp]
theorem res_zero {V W : Opens X} (h : V ≤ W) : res Q h 0 = 0 := map_zero _

/-- Restriction is additive, so it commutes with subtraction. -/
@[simp]
theorem res_sub {V W : Opens X} (h : V ≤ W) (s t : ToType (Q.obj (op W))) :
    res Q h (s - t) = res Q h s - res Q h t := map_sub _ _ _

/-- Restriction is additive. -/
theorem res_add {V W : Opens X} (h : V ≤ W) (s t : ToType (Q.obj (op W))) :
    res Q h (s + t) = res Q h s + res Q h t := map_add _ _ _

/-- Restriction is additive, so it commutes with finite sums. -/
theorem res_sum {V W : Opens X} (h : V ≤ W) {κ : Type*} (G : Finset κ)
    (f : κ → ToType (Q.obj (op W))) :
    res Q h (∑ i ∈ G, f i) = ∑ i ∈ G, res Q h (f i) := map_sum _ _ _

/-- Restriction is additive, so it commutes with integer multiples. -/
theorem res_zsmul {V W : Opens X} (h : V ≤ W) (n : ℤ) (s : ToType (Q.obj (op W))) :
    res Q h (n • s) = n • res Q h s := map_zsmul _ _ _

/-- Restriction commutes with a morphism of presheaves. -/
theorem res_app {Q' : (Opens X)ᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{v}} (φ : Q ⟶ Q') {V W : Opens X} (h : V ≤ W)
    (s : ToType (Q.obj (op W))) :
    res Q' h (ConcreteCategory.hom (φ.app (op W)) s) =
      ConcreteCategory.hom (φ.app (op V)) (res Q h s) := by
  simp only [res, ← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply]
  exact ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (φ.naturality (homOfLE h).op).symm s

/-- Restriction in the presheaf of underlying sets is `res`. -/
theorem forget_map_eq_res {V W : Opens X} (f : V ⟶ W)
    (s : (Q ⋙ forget AddCommGrpCat.{v}).obj (op W)) :
    (Q ⋙ forget AddCommGrpCat.{v}).map f.op s = res Q (leOfHom f) s := rfl

/-! ### The gluing and separatedness properties of a sheaf of abelian groups -/

/-- The sieve on `U` consisting of the open subsets contained in some member of a family. -/
@[sga "4½ Arcata 1.1"]
def coverSieve {ι : Type*} (V : ι → Opens X) (U : Opens X) : Sieve U where
  arrows W _ := ∃ i, W ≤ V i
  downward_closed := by
    rintro W W' f ⟨i, hi⟩ g
    exact ⟨i, (leOfHom g).trans hi⟩

/-- A family of opens covering `U` generates a covering sieve of `U`. -/
theorem coverSieve_mem {ι : Type*} {V : ι → Opens X} {U : Opens X} (hle : ∀ i, V i ≤ U)
    (hsup : U ≤ ⨆ i, V i) : coverSieve V U ∈ Opens.grothendieckTopology X U := by
  intro x hx
  obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := Opens.mem_iSup.1 (hsup hx)
  exact ⟨V i, homOfLE (hle i), ⟨i, le_refl _⟩, hi⟩

/-- An index of the family witnessing that an open belongs to `coverSieve`. -/
noncomputable def coverSieveIndex {ι : Type*} {V : ι → Opens X} {U W : Opens X} {f : W ⟶ U}
    (hf : (coverSieve V U).arrows f) : ι :=
  hf.choose

/-- The open witnessed by `coverSieveIndex` is contained in the corresponding member. -/
theorem le_coverSieveIndex {ι : Type*} {V : ι → Opens X} {U W : Opens X} {f : W ⟶ U}
    (hf : (coverSieve V U).arrows f) : W ≤ V (coverSieveIndex hf) :=
  hf.choose_spec

variable (P : Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) AddCommGrpCat.{v})

/-- **Separatedness.** Two sections of a sheaf of abelian groups over `U` that agree on the
members of a cover of `U` are equal. -/
theorem eq_of_res_eq {ι : Type*} (V : ι → Opens X) {U : Opens X} (hle : ∀ i, V i ≤ U)
    (hsup : U ≤ ⨆ i, V i) (s t : ToType (P.obj.obj (op U)))
    (h : ∀ i, res P.obj (hle i) s = res P.obj (hle i) t) : s = t := by
  refine P.isSeparated U (coverSieve V U) (coverSieve_mem hle hsup) s t ?_
  rintro W f ⟨i, hi⟩
  rw [res_eq_apply, res_eq_apply, ← res_res P.obj hi (hle i), ← res_res P.obj hi (hle i), h i]

/-- **Gluing.** A family of sections of a sheaf of abelian groups over the members of a cover
of `U` which agree on every open contained in two members glues to a section over `U`. -/
theorem exists_res_eq_of_compatible {ι : Type*} (V : ι → Opens X) {U : Opens X}
    (hle : ∀ i, V i ≤ U) (hsup : U ≤ ⨆ i, V i) (sf : ∀ i, ToType (P.obj.obj (op (V i))))
    (hc : ∀ (i j : ι) (Z : Opens X) (h₁ : Z ≤ V i) (h₂ : Z ≤ V j),
      res P.obj h₁ (sf i) = res P.obj h₂ (sf j)) :
    ∃ t : ToType (P.obj.obj (op U)), ∀ i, res P.obj (hle i) t = sf i := by
  have hty : Presieve.IsSheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology X)
      (P.obj ⋙ forget AddCommGrpCat.{v}) :=
    (isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type _ _).1
      ((sheafCompose (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) (forget AddCommGrpCat.{v})).obj P).2
  obtain ⟨t, ht, -⟩ := hty (coverSieve V U) (coverSieve_mem hle hsup)
    (fun W _ hf => res P.obj (le_coverSieveIndex hf) (sf (coverSieveIndex hf)))
    (by
      rintro Y₁ Y₂ Z g₁ g₂ f₁ f₂ h₁ h₂ -
      rw [forget_map_eq_res, forget_map_eq_res, res_res, res_res]
      exact hc _ _ _ _ _)
  refine ⟨t, fun i => ?_⟩
  have hmem : (coverSieve V U).arrows (homOfLE (hle i)) := ⟨i, le_refl _⟩
  calc res P.obj (hle i) t
      = res P.obj (le_coverSieveIndex hmem) (sf (coverSieveIndex hmem)) :=
        ht (homOfLE (hle i)) hmem
    _ = res P.obj (le_refl (V i)) (sf i) := hc _ i (V i) _ _
    _ = sf i := res_id P.obj (sf i)

/-- Evaluation of a sheaf of abelian groups at an open subset preserves finite limits. -/
instance evalPreservesFiniteLimits (W : Opens X) :
    PreservesFiniteLimits
      ((sheafSections (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) AddCommGrpCat.{v}).obj (op W)) := by
  rw [show (sheafSections (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) AddCommGrpCat.{v}).obj (op W)
      = sheafToPresheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) AddCommGrpCat.{v}
        ⋙ (evaluation (Opens X)ᵒᵖ AddCommGrpCat.{v}).obj (op W) from rfl]
  infer_instance

/-! ### Sections as morphisms from the integers -/

/-- A section of an abelian group, viewed as a morphism from the free abelian group on one
generator. -/
noncomputable def ofElt {A : AddCommGrpCat.{v}} (a : ToType A) :
    AddCommGrpCat.of (ULift.{v} ℤ) ⟶ A :=
  AddCommGrpCat.ofHom
    { toFun := fun m => m.down • a
      map_zero' := by simp
      map_add' := fun m n => by simp [add_zsmul] }

/-- The morphism attached to a section takes the generator to that section. -/
@[simp]
theorem ofElt_apply {A : AddCommGrpCat.{v}} (a : ToType A) :
    ConcreteCategory.hom (ofElt a) (ULift.up 1) = a := one_zsmul a

/-- Two morphisms out of the free abelian group on one generator agreeing on the generator are
equal. -/
theorem hom_ext_of_ulift_int {A : AddCommGrpCat.{v}}
    {f g : AddCommGrpCat.of (ULift.{v} ℤ) ⟶ A}
    (h : ConcreteCategory.hom f (ULift.up 1) = ConcreteCategory.hom g (ULift.up 1)) : f = g := by
  ext m
  have hm : m = m.down • (ULift.up 1 : ULift.{v} ℤ) := ULift.ext (by simp)
  rw [hm, map_zsmul, map_zsmul, h]

/-- `ofElt` is natural: composing with a morphism applies it to the section. -/
theorem ofElt_comp {A B : AddCommGrpCat.{v}} (a : ToType A) (f : A ⟶ B) :
    ofElt a ≫ f = ofElt (ConcreteCategory.hom f a) :=
  hom_ext_of_ulift_int (by rw [ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, ofElt_apply, ofElt_apply])

/-- `ofElt` is injective. -/
theorem eq_of_ofElt {A : AddCommGrpCat.{v}} {a b : ToType A} (h : ofElt a = ofElt b) : a = b := by
  rw [← ofElt_apply a, ← ofElt_apply b, h]

/-- Applying a finite sum of morphisms of abelian groups to a section. -/
theorem hom_sum_apply {A B : AddCommGrpCat.{v}} {κ : Type*} (G : Finset κ) (f : κ → (A ⟶ B))
    (s : ToType A) :
    ConcreteCategory.hom (∑ i ∈ G, f i) s = ∑ i ∈ G, ConcreteCategory.hom (f i) s := by
  classical
  induction G using Finset.induction with
  | empty => simp
  | insert a G ha ih =>
    rw [Finset.sum_insert ha, Finset.sum_insert ha, ← ih]
    rfl

/-! ### Sections of the Čech complex -/

section Cech

variable {κ : Type u} (Y : κ → Opens X) (P : (Opens X)ᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{v})
  [HasProducts.{u} AddCommGrpCat.{v}]

/-- A section of the degree-`n` term of the Čech complex with prescribed components. -/
noncomputable def cechMk (n : ℕ)
    (f : ∀ x : Fin (n + 1) → κ, ToType (P.obj (op (inter Y x)))) :
    ToType (((cechComplexFunctor Y).obj P).X n) :=
  ConcreteCategory.hom (lift Y P fun x => ofElt (f x)) (ULift.up 1)

/-- The components of `cechMk` are the prescribed sections. -/
@[simp]
theorem π_cechMk (n : ℕ) (f : ∀ x : Fin (n + 1) → κ, ToType (P.obj (op (inter Y x))))
    (x : Fin (n + 1) → κ) :
    ConcreteCategory.hom (π Y P n x) (cechMk Y P n f) = f x := by
  rw [cechMk, ← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, lift_comp_π, ofElt_apply]

/-- A section of the degree-`n` term of the Čech complex is determined by its components. -/
theorem cech_ext {n : ℕ} (s t : ToType (((cechComplexFunctor Y).obj P).X n))
    (h : ∀ x, ConcreteCategory.hom (π Y P n x) s = ConcreteCategory.hom (π Y P n x) t) : s = t :=
  eq_of_ofElt (Stacks.CategoryTheory.CechComplex.hom_ext Y P fun x => by
    rw [ofElt_comp, ofElt_comp, h x])

end Cech

/-! ### Left exactness in element form -/

/-- A functor to abelian groups which preserves kernels turns a kernel fork into an exact
sequence of abelian groups: a section of the middle term killed by the second map is the image
of a section of the first term. -/
theorem exists_map_eq_of_isLimit_kernelFork {C : Type*} [Category C] [HasZeroMorphisms C]
    (G : C ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{v}) [G.PreservesZeroMorphisms] [PreservesFiniteLimits G]
    {A B D : C} (f : A ⟶ B) (g : B ⟶ D) (w : f ≫ g = 0)
    (hlim : IsLimit (KernelFork.ofι f w)) (b : ToType (G.obj B))
    (hb : ConcreteCategory.hom (G.map g) b = 0) :
    ∃ a, ConcreteCategory.hom (G.map f) a = b := by
  have hex : (ShortComplex.mk f g w |>.map G).Exact :=
    ShortComplex.exact_of_f_is_kernel _ (KernelFork.mapIsLimit _ hlim G)
  exact (ShortComplex.ab_exact_iff _).1 hex b hb

/-! ### Coefficients over the abelian sheaves on a space

From here on the coefficients are an arbitrary abelian category `𝒜` equipped with an exact
functor `T` to the abelian sheaves on `X` — the "underlying abelian sheaf" of a coefficient
object.  Sheaves of modules over a sheaf of rings `R` are the case `T = SheafOfModules.toSheaf R`
and abelian sheaves themselves are the case `T = 𝟭`; only these two facts about `T` are used,
namely that it is exact and that it carries injective objects to Čech-acyclic sheaves. -/

variable {𝒜 : Type u₂} [Category.{v₂} 𝒜] [Abelian 𝒜]
  (T : 𝒜 ⥤ Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) AddCommGrpCat.{max u w})

/-- The presheaf of abelian groups underlying a coefficient object. -/
noncomputable abbrev abPresheaf (A : 𝒜) : (Opens X)ᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{max u w} :=
  (T.obj A).obj

/-- Sections over an open subset of the abelian sheaf underlying a coefficient object, as a
functor of the coefficients.  For sheaves of modules this is `secF`. -/
noncomputable abbrev secFunctor (W : Opens X) : 𝒜 ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{max u w} :=
  T ⋙ (sheafSections (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) AddCommGrpCat.{max u w}).obj (op W)

/-- The map on sections over an open subset induced by a morphism of coefficients. -/
noncomputable def sec {A A' : 𝒜} (g : A ⟶ A') (W : Opens X)
    (s : ToType ((abPresheaf T A).obj (op W))) : ToType ((abPresheaf T A').obj (op W)) :=
  ConcreteCategory.hom ((T.map g).hom.app (op W)) s

section Sec

omit [Abelian 𝒜]

variable {A A' A'' : 𝒜} (g : A ⟶ A') (W : Opens X)

/-- Restriction commutes with the maps induced by a morphism of coefficients. -/
theorem res_sec {V : Opens X} (h : V ≤ W) (s : ToType ((abPresheaf T A).obj (op W))) :
    res (abPresheaf T A') h (sec T g W s) = sec T g V (res (abPresheaf T A) h s) :=
  res_app _ (T.map g).hom h s

/-- The map induced on sections by a morphism of coefficients preserves zero. -/
@[simp]
theorem sec_zero : sec T g W 0 = 0 := map_zero _

/-- The map induced on sections by a morphism of coefficients is additive. -/
@[simp]
theorem sec_add (s t : ToType ((abPresheaf T A).obj (op W))) :
    sec T g W (s + t) = sec T g W s + sec T g W t := map_add _ _ _

/-- The map induced on sections commutes with subtraction. -/
@[simp]
theorem sec_sub (s t : ToType ((abPresheaf T A).obj (op W))) :
    sec T g W (s - t) = sec T g W s - sec T g W t := map_sub _ _ _

/-- The map induced on sections commutes with integer multiples. -/
theorem sec_zsmul (n : ℤ) (s : ToType ((abPresheaf T A).obj (op W))) :
    sec T g W (n • s) = n • sec T g W s := map_zsmul _ _ _

/-- The maps on sections induced by a composite. -/
theorem sec_sec (g' : A' ⟶ A'') (s : ToType ((abPresheaf T A).obj (op W))) :
    sec T g' W (sec T g W s) = sec T (g ≫ g') W s := by
  simp only [sec, ← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, ← NatTrans.comp_app,
    ← ObjectProperty.FullSubcategory.comp_hom, ← Functor.map_comp]

end Sec

/-! ### Additivity and left exactness of the coefficient functor -/

variable [T.Additive]

/-- The zero morphism of coefficients induces the zero map on sections. -/
theorem sec_of_zero {A A' : 𝒜} (W : Opens X) (s : ToType ((abPresheaf T A).obj (op W))) :
    sec T (0 : A ⟶ A') W s = 0 := by
  rw [sec, Functor.map_zero]
  rfl

/-- Sections over an open subset are additive in the coefficients. -/
instance secFunctorAdditive (W : Opens X) : (secFunctor T W).Additive := by
  unfold secFunctor; infer_instance

variable [PreservesFiniteLimits T]

/-- The sections functor over an open subset preserves finite limits. -/
instance secFunctorPreservesFiniteLimits (W : Opens X) :
    PreservesFiniteLimits (secFunctor T W) :=
  comp_preservesFiniteLimits _ _

/-! ### Sections of an injective resolution -/

/-- The augmentation of an injective resolution, as a morphism out of the resolved object. -/
noncomputable def resolutionι {F : 𝒜} (I : InjectiveResolution F) : F ⟶ I.cocomplex.X 0 :=
  I.ι.f 0

/-- The augmentation of an injective resolution is killed by the first differential. -/
theorem resolutionι_comp_d {F : 𝒜} (I : InjectiveResolution F) :
    resolutionι I ≫ I.cocomplex.d 0 1 = 0 :=
  I.ι_f_zero_comp_complex_d

/-- The resolved object is the kernel of the first differential of the resolution. -/
noncomputable def isLimitKernelForkι {F : 𝒜} (I : InjectiveResolution F) :
    IsLimit (KernelFork.ofι (resolutionι I) (resolutionι_comp_d I)) :=
  I.isLimitKernelFork

/-- The map on sections induced by the inclusion of a kernel is injective. -/
theorem injective_sec_of_isLimit {G A A' : 𝒜} (ιG : G ⟶ A) {dA : A ⟶ A'}
    (hzero : ιG ≫ dA = 0) (hker : IsLimit (KernelFork.ofι ιG hzero)) (W : Opens X) :
    Function.Injective (sec T ιG W) := by
  have hmono : Mono ((secFunctor T W).map ιG) :=
    mono_of_isLimit_fork (KernelFork.mapIsLimit _ hker (secFunctor T W))
  exact (AddCommGrpCat.mono_iff_injective _).mp hmono

/-- A section killed by a morphism of coefficients is the image of a section of its kernel. -/
theorem exists_sec_eq_of_isLimit {G A A' : 𝒜} (ιG : G ⟶ A) {dA : A ⟶ A'}
    (hzero : ιG ≫ dA = 0) (hker : IsLimit (KernelFork.ofι ιG hzero)) (W : Opens X)
    (s : ToType ((abPresheaf T A).obj (op W))) (hs : sec T dA W s = 0) :
    ∃ a : ToType ((abPresheaf T G).obj (op W)), sec T ιG W a = s :=
  exists_map_eq_of_isLimit_kernelFork (secFunctor T W) ιG dA hzero hker s hs

variable [PreservesFiniteColimits T]
  [HasSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) AddCommGrpCat.{max u w}]
  [(Opens.grothendieckTopology X).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{max u w}]

omit [HasSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) AddCommGrpCat.{max u w}]
  [(Opens.grothendieckTopology X).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{max u w}] in
/-- **The coefficient functor carries an injective resolution to an exact complex of abelian
sheaves.**  The resolution is exact in positive degrees and `T` is exact.  For sheaves of modules
this is `toSheaf_cocomplex_exactAt`. -/
theorem map_cocomplex_exactAt {F : 𝒜} (I : InjectiveResolution F) (k : ℕ) :
    ((T.mapHomologicalComplex _).obj I.cocomplex).ExactAt (k + 1) := by
  rw [HomologicalComplex.exactAt_iff]
  have h : I.cocomplex.ExactAt (k + 1) := I.cocomplex_exactAt_succ k
  rw [HomologicalComplex.exactAt_iff] at h
  exact h.map T

/-- **Local primitives.** A section over `U` of the degree-`n + 1` term of an injective
resolution which is killed by the next differential is, on the members of some open cover of
`U`, the image under the differential of a section of the degree-`n` term. -/
theorem exists_cover_res_eq_d {F : 𝒜} (I : InjectiveResolution F) (U : Opens X)
    (n : ℕ) (z : ToType ((abPresheaf T (I.cocomplex.X (n + 1))).obj (op U)))
    (hz : sec T (I.cocomplex.d (n + 1) (n + 2)) U z = 0) :
    ∃ (J : Type u) (V : J → Opens X) (hle : ∀ j, V j ≤ U), (⨆ j, V j) = U ∧
      ∀ j, ∃ y : ToType ((abPresheaf T (I.cocomplex.X n)).obj (op (V j))),
        sec T (I.cocomplex.d n (n + 1)) (V j) y
          = res (abPresheaf T (I.cocomplex.X (n + 1))) (hle j) z := by
  classical
  set S : ShortComplex (Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) AddCommGrpCat.{max u w}) :=
    ((T.mapHomologicalComplex _).obj I.cocomplex).sc' n (n + 1) (n + 2)
    with hS
  have hex : S.Exact := by
    rw [hS]
    exact (HomologicalComplex.exactAt_iff' _ n (n + 1) (n + 2) (by simp)
      (by simp [CochainComplex.next])).1 (map_cocomplex_exactAt T I n)
  have hpls : Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) S.toCycles.hom :=
    (Sheaf.isLocallySurjective_iff_epi' AddCommGrpCat S.toCycles).mpr hex.epi_toCycles
  obtain ⟨z', hz'⟩ := exists_map_eq_of_isLimit_kernelFork
    ((sheafSections (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) AddCommGrpCat.{max u w}).obj (op U))
    S.iCycles S.g S.iCycles_g S.cyclesIsKernel z hz
  obtain ⟨J, V, hle, harrow, hsup⟩ := exists_opens_cover_of_mem_grothendieckTopology U
    (Presheaf.imageSieve S.toCycles.hom z')
    (Presheaf.imageSieve_mem (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) _ (U := op U) z')
  refine ⟨J, V, hle, hsup, fun j => ?_⟩
  refine ⟨Presheaf.localPreimage S.toCycles.hom z' (homOfLE (hle j)) (harrow j), ?_⟩
  have happ := Presheaf.app_localPreimage S.toCycles.hom z' (homOfLE (hle j)) (harrow j)
  have hfac : S.toCycles.hom ≫ S.iCycles.hom = S.f.hom := by
    rw [← ObjectProperty.FullSubcategory.comp_hom, S.toCycles_i]
  have hz'' : ConcreteCategory.hom (S.iCycles.hom.app (op U)) z' = z := hz'
  have key := congrArg (ConcreteCategory.hom (S.iCycles.hom.app (op (V j)))) happ
  rwa [← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, ← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, ← NatTrans.comp_app, hfac,
    S.iCycles.hom.naturality (homOfLE (hle j)).op, ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, hz''] at key

/-! ### The Čech-to-cohomology comparison in degree one -/

omit [PreservesFiniteColimits T]
  [HasSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) AddCommGrpCat.{max u w}]
  [(Opens.grothendieckTopology X).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{max u w}] in
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 200000 in
set_option maxHeartbeats 1600000 in
/-- **Čech-to-cohomology in degree one.** Let `ιG : G ⟶ A` be a kernel of `dA : A ⟶ A'`, let `W`
be an open cover of an open subset, let `z` be a section of `A'` over `W.carrier`, and suppose
that on each member of `W` the section `z` is the image under `dA` of a section `u k` of `A`.
If the degree-one Čech cohomology of `G` for the cover `W` vanishes, then `z` is already the
image under `dA` of a section over `W.carrier`.

The proof is the classical one: the differences `u k - u l` over the pairwise intersections are
killed by `dA`, hence come from sections of `G`; these assemble into a Čech `1`-cocycle, which
the Čech vanishing hypothesis exhibits as the coboundary of a Čech `0`-cochain; subtracting that
cochain from the family `u` makes it compatible, and the sheaf condition glues it.

Applied to the augmentation `F ⟶ I⁰` of an injective resolution this is the degree-one
Čech-to-cohomology comparison; applied to the inclusion of the sheaf of `m`-cocycles
`Zᵐ ⟶ Iᵐ` it is the comparison in degree `m + 1`. -/
theorem exists_sec_eq_of_cech_isZero {G A A' : 𝒜} (ιG : G ⟶ A) {dA : A ⟶ A'}
    (hzero : ιG ≫ dA = 0) (hker : IsLimit (KernelFork.ofι ιG hzero))
    (W : OpenCover X)
    (hW : IsZero (((cechComplexFunctor W.obj).obj (abPresheaf T G)).homology 1))
    (z : ToType ((abPresheaf T A').obj (op W.carrier)))
    (u : ∀ k, ToType ((abPresheaf T A).obj (op (W.obj k))))
    (hu : ∀ k, sec T dA (W.obj k) (u k) = res (abPresheaf T A') (W.obj_le k) z) :
    ∃ t : ToType ((abPresheaf T A).obj (op W.carrier)), sec T dA W.carrier t = z := by
  classical
  have hint : ∀ {m : ℕ} (y : Fin m → W.ι) (a : Fin m), inter W.obj y ≤ W.obj (y a) :=
    fun y a => leOfHom (interπ W.obj y a)
  -- The differences of the local primitives come from sections of `F`.
  have hg : ∀ y : Fin 2 → W.ι, ∃ a : ToType ((abPresheaf T G).obj (op (inter W.obj y))),
      sec T (ιG) (inter W.obj y) a
        = res (abPresheaf T A) (hint y 1) (u (y 1))
          - res (abPresheaf T A) (hint y 0) (u (y 0)) := by
    intro y
    refine exists_sec_eq_of_isLimit T ιG hzero hker _ _ ?_
    rw [sec_sub, ← res_sec, ← res_sec, hu, hu, res_res, res_res]
    exact sub_eq_zero_of_eq rfl
  choose c hc using hg
  -- The family `c` is a Čech `1`-cocycle.
  have hcocycle : ConcreteCategory.hom
      (((cechComplexFunctor W.obj).obj (abPresheaf T G)).d 1 2)
      (cechMk W.obj (abPresheaf T G) 1 c) = 0 := by
    refine cech_ext W.obj (abPresheaf T G) _ _ fun y => ?_
    rw [map_zero, ← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, d_comp_π, hom_sum_apply, Fin.sum_univ_three]
    refine injective_sec_of_isLimit T ιG hzero hker (inter W.obj y) ?_
    set p : Fin 3 → ToType ((abPresheaf T A).obj (op (inter W.obj y))) :=
      fun a => res (abPresheaf T A) (hint y a) (u (y a))
    have hv : ∀ i : Fin 3, sec T ιG (inter W.obj y)
        (ConcreteCategory.hom ((-1 : ℤ) ^ (i : ℕ) •
          (π W.obj (abPresheaf T G) 1 (y ∘ i.succAbove) ≫
            (abPresheaf T G).map (interMap W.obj y i.succAbove).op))
          (cechMk W.obj (abPresheaf T G) 1 c))
        = (-1 : ℤ) ^ (i : ℕ) • (p (i.succAbove 1) - p (i.succAbove 0)) := by
      intro i
      change sec T ιG _ ((-1 : ℤ) ^ (i : ℕ) • _) = _
      rw [sec_zsmul, ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, π_cechMk, res_eq_apply, ← res_sec, hc, res_sub,
        res_res, res_res]
      rfl
    rw [sec_zero, sec_add, sec_add, hv 0, hv 1, hv 2]
    simp [Fin.succAbove, p]
  -- Čech vanishing writes the cocycle as a coboundary.
  have hexact : (((cechComplexFunctor W.obj).obj (abPresheaf T G)).sc' 0 1 2).Exact := by
    rwa [← HomologicalComplex.exactAt_iff' _ 0 1 2 (by simp) (by simp [CochainComplex.next]),
      HomologicalComplex.exactAt_iff_isZero_homology]
  obtain ⟨b0, hb0⟩ := (ShortComplex.ab_exact_iff _).1 hexact _ hcocycle
  obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ : ∃ b : ToType (((cechComplexFunctor W.obj).obj (abPresheaf T G)).X 0),
      ConcreteCategory.hom (((cechComplexFunctor W.obj).obj (abPresheaf T G)).d 0 1) b
        = cechMk W.obj (abPresheaf T G) 1 c := ⟨b0, hb0⟩
  -- The cocycle is the Čech coboundary of the family of components of `b`.
  have hcob : ∀ y : Fin 2 → W.ι, c y
      = res (abPresheaf T G) (leOfHom (interMap W.obj y fun _ => 1))
          (ConcreteCategory.hom (π W.obj (abPresheaf T G) 0 (fun _ => y 1)) b)
        - res (abPresheaf T G) (leOfHom (interMap W.obj y fun _ => 0))
          (ConcreteCategory.hom (π W.obj (abPresheaf T G) 0 (fun _ => y 0)) b) := by
    intro y
    rw [← π_cechMk W.obj _ 1 c y, ← hb, ← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, d_zero_comp_π]
    rfl
  -- Correct the local primitives by the Čech `0`-cochain and glue.
  have hV'le : ∀ k, inter W.obj (fun _ : Fin 1 => k) ≤ W.carrier :=
    fun k => (hint (fun _ : Fin 1 => k) 0).trans (W.obj_le k)
  have hV'sup : W.carrier ≤ ⨆ k, inter W.obj (fun _ : Fin 1 => k) := by
    refine le_of_eq ?_
    rw [← W.iSup_eq]
    exact (iSup_congr fun k => inter_eq_single W.obj fun _ => k).symm
  obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := exists_res_eq_of_compatible
    (T.obj A) _ hV'le hV'sup
    (fun k => res (abPresheaf T A) (hint (fun _ : Fin 1 => k) 0) (u k)
      - sec T (ιG) (inter W.obj (fun _ : Fin 1 => k))
          (ConcreteCategory.hom (π W.obj (abPresheaf T G) 0 (fun _ => k)) b))
    (by
      intro k l Z h₁ h₂
      set y : Fin 2 → W.ι := fun m => if m = 0 then k else l with hy
      have hy0 : y 0 = k := rfl
      have hy1 : y 1 = l := rfl
      have hZy : Z ≤ inter W.obj y := by
        rw [inter_eq_inf, hy0, hy1]
        exact le_inf (h₁.trans (hint (fun _ : Fin 1 => k) 0))
          (h₂.trans (hint (fun _ : Fin 1 => l) 0))
      have hk : inter W.obj y ≤ inter W.obj (fun _ : Fin 1 => k) :=
        leOfHom (interMap W.obj y fun _ => 0)
      have hl : inter W.obj y ≤ inter W.obj (fun _ : Fin 1 => l) :=
        leOfHom (interMap W.obj y fun _ => 1)
      rw [← res_res _ hZy hk, ← res_res _ hZy hl]
      congr 1
      have hkey : res (abPresheaf T A) (hint y 1) (u (y 1))
          - res (abPresheaf T A) (hint y 0) (u (y 0))
          = sec T (ιG) (inter W.obj y)
              (res (abPresheaf T G) hl
                (ConcreteCategory.hom (π W.obj (abPresheaf T G) 0 (fun _ => l)) b))
            - sec T (ιG) (inter W.obj y)
              (res (abPresheaf T G) hk
                (ConcreteCategory.hom (π W.obj (abPresheaf T G) 0 (fun _ => k)) b)) := by
        rw [← hc y, hcob y, sec_sub]
        rfl
      rw [res_sub, res_sub, res_sec, res_sec, res_res, res_res]
      exact (sub_eq_sub_iff_sub_eq_sub.mp hkey).symm)
  refine ⟨t, eq_of_res_eq (T.obj A') _ hV'le hV'sup _ _ fun k => ?_⟩
  rw [res_sec, ht, sec_sub, ← res_sec, hu, res_res, sec_sec, hzero, sec_of_zero,
    sub_zero]

/-! ### Vanishing of higher cohomology on a basis -/

variable [EnoughInjectives 𝒜]

/-- The cohomology of a coefficient object over an open subset: the right-derived functors of
sections.  For sheaves of modules this is `Hgroup`. -/
noncomputable abbrev Hobj (W : Opens X) (n : ℕ) (A : 𝒜) : AddCommGrpCat.{max u w} :=
  ((secFunctor T W).rightDerived n).obj A

/-- The complex of sections of an injective resolution over an open subset.  For sheaves of
modules this is `secCx`. -/
noncomputable abbrev secComplex {F : 𝒜} (I : InjectiveResolution F) (W : Opens X) :
    CochainComplex AddCommGrpCat.{max u w} ℕ :=
  ((secFunctor T W).mapHomologicalComplex _).obj I.cocomplex

set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 200000 in
/-- **Vanishing of `Hᵐ⁺¹` from degree-one Čech vanishing for the `m`-cocycles.**
Fix an injective resolution `I` of `F` and a coefficient object `G` realized as a kernel of the
`m`-th differential of `I`, so that `G` is the object of `m`-cocycles of the resolution.  If every
open cover of an open subset `U` of `B` is refined by a member of `Cov` covering `U` and the
degree-one Čech cohomology of `G` vanishes for every member of `Cov`, then `Hᵐ⁺¹(U, F)`
vanishes.

For `m = 0` the object of `0`-cocycles is `F` itself, and this is the degree-one statement
`isZero_Hobj_one_of_cech_isZero`. -/
theorem isZero_Hobj_succ_of_cech_isZero {F : 𝒜} (I : InjectiveResolution F)
    (m : ℕ) {G : 𝒜} (ιG : G ⟶ I.cocomplex.X m)
    (hzero : ιG ≫ I.cocomplex.d m (m + 1) = 0)
    (hker : IsLimit (KernelFork.ofι ιG hzero)) (B : Set (Opens X)) (Cov : Set (OpenCover X))
    (hCovCofinal : ∀ U ∈ B, ∀ V : OpenCover X, V.carrier = U →
      ∃ W ∈ Cov, W.carrier = U ∧ W.Refines V)
    (hCech : ∀ W ∈ Cov, IsZero (((cechComplexFunctor W.obj).obj (abPresheaf T G)).homology 1))
    (U : Opens X) (hU : U ∈ B) :
    IsZero (Hobj T U (m + 1) F) := by
  classical
  refine IsZero.of_iso ?_ (I.isoRightDerivedObj (secFunctor T U) (m + 1))
  rw [AddCommGrpCat.isZero_iff_subsingleton]
  refine subsingleton_of_forall_eq 0 fun ξ => ?_
  obtain ⟨cy, hcy⟩ := (AddCommGrpCat.epi_iff_surjective
    ((secComplex T I U).homologyπ (m + 1))).mp inferInstance ξ
  have hdz : sec T (I.cocomplex.d (m + 1) (m + 2)) U
      (ConcreteCategory.hom ((secComplex T I U).iCycles (m + 1)) cy) = 0 :=
    (ConcreteCategory.congr_hom ((secComplex T I U).iCycles_d (m + 1) (m + 2)) cy).trans rfl
  obtain ⟨Jx, V, hle, hsup, hprim⟩ := exists_cover_res_eq_d T I U m _ hdz
  choose y hy using hprim
  obtain ⟨W, hWmem, hWcar, hWref⟩ := hCovCofinal U hU ⟨Jx, U, V, hsup⟩ rfl
  choose σ hσ using hWref.2
  subst hWcar
  have hu : ∀ k, sec T (I.cocomplex.d m (m + 1)) (W.obj k)
      (res (abPresheaf T (I.cocomplex.X m)) (hσ k) (y (σ k)))
      = res (abPresheaf T (I.cocomplex.X (m + 1))) (W.obj_le k)
        (ConcreteCategory.hom ((secComplex T I W.carrier).iCycles (m + 1)) cy) := by
    intro k
    rw [← res_sec, hy, res_res]
  obtain ⟨t, htz⟩ := exists_sec_eq_of_cech_isZero T ιG hzero hker W (hCech W hWmem) _ _ hu
  have hmono : Function.Injective
      (ConcreteCategory.hom ((secComplex T I W.carrier).iCycles (m + 1))) := by
    rw [← AddCommGrpCat.mono_iff_injective]
    infer_instance
  have heq : cy = ConcreteCategory.hom ((secComplex T I W.carrier).toCycles m (m + 1)) t :=
    hmono (by
      rw [← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, (secComplex T I W.carrier).toCycles_i]
      exact htz.symm)
  rw [← hcy, heq, ← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply,
    (secComplex T I W.carrier).toCycles_comp_homologyπ]
  rfl

set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 200000 in
/-- **Vanishing of `H¹` from Čech vanishing.** If every open cover of an open subset `U` in `B`
is refined by a member of `Cov` covering `U`, and the degree-one Čech cohomology of `F` vanishes
for every member of `Cov`, then `H¹(U, F)` vanishes. -/
theorem isZero_Hobj_one_of_cech_isZero (F : 𝒜) (B : Set (Opens X))
    (Cov : Set (OpenCover X))
    (hCovCofinal : ∀ U ∈ B, ∀ V : OpenCover X, V.carrier = U →
      ∃ W ∈ Cov, W.carrier = U ∧ W.Refines V)
    (hCech : ∀ W ∈ Cov, IsZero (((cechComplexFunctor W.obj).obj (abPresheaf T F)).homology 1))
    (U : Opens X) (hU : U ∈ B) :
    IsZero (Hobj T U 1 F) :=
  isZero_Hobj_succ_of_cech_isZero T (.of F) 0 _ _ (isLimitKernelForkι _) B Cov hCovCofinal
    hCech U hU

set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 200000 in
/-- **The degree-one case of Stacks Tag 01EW**, stated with the hypotheses of the general
result.  Neither the basis hypothesis on `B` nor the closure of `B` under the intersections
occurring in the Čech complexes is needed in degree one; they are kept so that this is literally
the case `n = 1` of Tag 01EW. -/
theorem isZero_Hobj_one_of_cech_isZero_on_basis (F : 𝒜) (B : Set (Opens X))
    (_hB : Opens.IsBasis B) (Cov : Set (OpenCover X))
    (_hCovBasis : ∀ U ∈ Cov, U.carrier ∈ B ∧ (∀ i, U.obj i ∈ B) ∧
      ∀ (p : ℕ) (s : Fin (p + 1) → U.ι), (⨅ k, U.obj (s k)) ∈ B)
    (hCovCofinal : ∀ U ∈ B, ∀ V : OpenCover X, V.carrier = U →
      ∃ W ∈ Cov, W.carrier = U ∧ W.Refines V)
    (hCech : ∀ U ∈ Cov, ∀ n : ℕ, 0 < n →
      IsZero (((cechComplexFunctor U.obj).obj (abPresheaf T F)).homology n))
    (U : Opens X) (hU : U ∈ B) :
    IsZero (Hobj T U 1 F) :=
  isZero_Hobj_one_of_cech_isZero T F B Cov hCovCofinal
    (fun W hW => hCech W hW 1 Nat.one_pos) U hU

set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 200000 in
/-- **Stacks Tag 01EW, modulo the degree-one Čech vanishing for the cocycles of an injective
resolution.**  Assume the hypotheses of Tag 01EW, and in addition that for every `m > 0` and
every cover in `Cov` the degree-one Čech cohomology of the object of `m`-cocycles
`Zᵐ = ker(Iᵐ → Iᵐ⁺¹)` of an injective resolution `I` of `F` vanishes.  Then higher cohomology
vanishes over every member of the basis.

The hypothesis `hCechCycles` is the only input missing for Tag 01EW itself.  Its classical
derivation is a cochain staircase: a Čech `p`-cocycle with values in `Zᵐ` lifts, degreewise, to
`Č ᵖ(𝒰, Iᵐ⁻¹)` because `Hᵐ(V, F)` vanishes on the intersections `V` occurring in the Čech
complex, which is why `hCovBasis` asks those intersections to lie in `B`; the Čech differential
of the lift is a cocycle with values in `Zᵐ⁻¹`, and downward recursion on `m` ends at
`Ȟ ⁿ(𝒰, F) = 0`, which is `hCech`.  Closing the recursion also uses that the positive-degree
Čech cohomology of the injective terms of the resolution vanishes. -/
theorem isZero_Hobj_of_cechCycles_isZero (F : 𝒜) (B : Set (Opens X))
    (_hB : Opens.IsBasis B) (Cov : Set (OpenCover X))
    (_hCovBasis : ∀ U ∈ Cov, U.carrier ∈ B ∧ (∀ i, U.obj i ∈ B) ∧
      ∀ (p : ℕ) (s : Fin (p + 1) → U.ι), (⨅ k, U.obj (s k)) ∈ B)
    (hCovCofinal : ∀ U ∈ B, ∀ V : OpenCover X, V.carrier = U →
      ∃ W ∈ Cov, W.carrier = U ∧ W.Refines V)
    (hCech : ∀ U ∈ Cov, ∀ n : ℕ, 0 < n →
      IsZero (((cechComplexFunctor U.obj).obj (abPresheaf T F)).homology n))
    (I : InjectiveResolution F)
    (hCechCycles : ∀ m : ℕ, 0 < m → ∀ W ∈ Cov,
      IsZero (((cechComplexFunctor W.obj).obj
        (abPresheaf T (I.cocomplex.cycles m))).homology 1))
    (U : Opens X) (hU : U ∈ B) (n : ℕ) (hn : 0 < n) :
    IsZero (Hobj T U n F) := by
  obtain ⟨m, rfl⟩ := Nat.exists_eq_succ_of_ne_zero hn.ne'
  rcases Nat.eq_zero_or_pos m with rfl | hm
  · exact isZero_Hobj_one_of_cech_isZero_on_basis T F B _hB Cov _hCovBasis hCovCofinal hCech U hU
  · exact isZero_Hobj_succ_of_cech_isZero T I m (I.cocomplex.iCycles m)
      (I.cocomplex.iCycles_d m (m + 1)) (I.cocomplex.cyclesIsKernel m (m + 1) (by simp))
      B Cov hCovCofinal (hCechCycles m hm) U hU

end Stacks.Cohomology.Basis

